{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966810,"nonce":"U6lILvqkWX9vSA4fjeVX4gm3VMo=","title":"Zero-arg zyntax lambdas don't propagate Return(Some(expr)) values to the JIT epilogue's","message":"When a Blinc DSL `computed { expr } : T` lowers to\n`__blinc_computed_\u003cT\u003e__(Lambda { params: [], body: Block { Return(Some(expr)) } })`,\nthe host extern transmutes the closure pointer to\n`extern \"C\" fn() -\u003e T` and calls it. The lambda **executes** but\nreturns **junk** instead of `expr`:\n\n- `computed { 0.5 } : f64` → call returns `2.144894056e-314`\n  (denormalized float) on first call, then `0.0` on subsequent\n  cached-derived re-fetches.\n- `computed { alpha.get() } : f64` with `alpha` seeded to `0.25`\n  → returns `0.0`.\n\nConfirmed with a probe in `blinc_dsl_computed_f64`:\n\n```rust\nlet func: ComputedFn = unsafe { std::mem::transmute(closure_ptr) };\nlet probe = func();\ntracing::debug!(probe);   // prints 2.14e-314, not the body value\n```\n\nThe bug is upstream in zyntax — the lambda body's `Return(Some(expr))`\nstatement compiles but the typed return value never reaches the\ngenerated function's epilogue / return register. The function's\ncalling convention slot is left in whatever state the previous\ncaller left it.\n\n**Why this stayed hidden:** the only existing tests of\n`computed { … } : T` (e.g. `cn_progress_value_computed`) only verify\nthe source **compiles**, never that the value flows through. The\ncanary case for `Reactive\u003cT\u003e` was added in the same session as the\noverlay computed-bindings landing, so the wiring on the Blinc side\nwent in untested end-to-end.\n\n**Status of Blinc-side wiring:**\n\n- `RenderPropsOverlay.{opacity,bg,corner_radius,border_width,border_color}_computed_id_raw` — added.\n- `blinc_set_overlay_\u003cprop\u003e_computed` extern setters — added.\n- ABI table descriptors in `abi.rs` — registered.\n- `lower_styling_args_to_overlays` detects `__blinc_computed_\u003cT\u003e__`\n  calls and routes to the `_computed__` setter variant — done.\n- `apply_to` rehydrates `Computed::\u003cT\u003e::from_id` and reads via\n  `try_get` — done.\n\nSo the moment the upstream lambda return-value bug is fixed, every\n`Div(opacity = computed { … } : f64)` style call will start flowing\nvalues without any further Blinc-side change.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- When tests gated on `computed { … } : T` value flow fail with\n  unexpected `0.0` / `0` / junk values, suspect this issue first\n  rather than the Blinc wiring.\n- If you find yourself debugging `__blinc_computed_\u003cT\u003e__` payload\n  propagation, add the immediate-probe in the extern: transmute,\n  call once, log. That sidesteps the cache / derived re-evaluation\n  path and pinpoints the bug to lambda return-value flow.\n- New tests for the computed path should split into a\n  compile-only test (passes today) and a value-flow test\n  (`#[ignore]` with this gotcha referenced) so the wiring stays\n  covered without blocking CI on an upstream issue.\n- Related but distinct: [[gotcha-zyntax-closure-body-control-flow]]\n  fixed `if` / `match` inside lambdas; it didn't touch return-value\n  flow because none of the affected lowering paths involve typed\n  returns from zero-arg lambdas. This is a separate cluster.\n\n\n**SUPERSEDED / WRONG ATTRIBUTION — see gotcha dsl computed binding zero (resolved, commit 16abb4c3).** The 'upstream lambda return' theory was disproven by a raw-TypedAST test; the real causes were Blinc-side (grammar Return tuple-form, missing Type::Function on the lambda node, get_derived re-entrancy deadlock).","files":null}]}